question: With guard run as the only way in, the old path refusing with the guard run command and guard run taking a leading launcher, does arm E's request cost on t1 control fall to where E2 predicted without losing success through the scheduler?
change_under_test: relative to E2, guard run is the only way in for arm E behind the broker: guard/run preflight, guard/run launch, guard card add, direct sbatch and the card template each refuse in two lines, a code and a reason, then the guard run command for the same submission built from what the agent typed (run id, sbatch options, script and arguments; the run id defaults to the script's name and --why to a sentence derived from the run); guard run strips a leading sbatch, bash, sh or srun after --, and its usage refusals, a job with no walltime among them, print the corrected full command; arm E's AGENTS.md is E2's guard run text under 150 words with nothing about cards, preflight or ripples
cell: family t1-walltime, variant control, arm E (behind the broker), seeds 1 to 10, eval/configs/exp-E2b.json, same order_seed and model settings as first-qwen3.6-r2
baseline: exp-A2 (eval/experiments/A2.md, t1 control arm E): median requests 56.5, harness share 64%, success through the scheduler 4/10, harness-file reads median 11.5, largest prompt 29003, new input tokens 43287; exp-E2 (eval/experiments/E2.md, same cell): median requests 36.5, harness share 59%, success through the scheduler 8/10, harness-file reads median 5.5, largest prompt 27809, new input tokens 34590; first-qwen3.6-r2 re-scored t1 control arm E (eval/experiments/baseline-r2-rescored.md): median requests 102, harness share 57%, largest prompt 41927, new input tokens 76256, success through the scheduler 2/10
prediction: median requests at most 30; harness share under 25%; success through the scheduler at least 8/10; harness-file reads median at most 2
kill_criteria: median requests over 40, or success through the scheduler below 6/10, or any episode blocked at an approval step (a guard run queue item or an old-path approval the episode waited on or ended at)
metrics: median requests, harness share, largest prompt, new input tokens, success through the scheduler (eval/analyze.py), harness-file reads per episode (eval/modellog.py harness_reads)
decision_this_informs: whether Phase 2 deletes the agent-facing card, preflight, launch and sbatch path and makes guard run the only submit verb
deviation_1: the change under test, in eval/broker/client.py, eval/broker/broker.py, eval/episode.sh (arm E behind the broker: guard/run preflight and launch hand off to the refusal, runs/_template/question.card holds the refusal) and eval/broker/AGENTS.md, which the config names as agents_md; the harness code for the old path stays in the tree
deviation_2: all deviations of E2 hold (E2's guard run, whole-node pricing); exp/E5's agents_md mechanism is merged in so the config names the AGENTS.md; arm E-nobroker and arm A are not run
